            "text": "{\n  \"units\": [\n    {\n      \"quote_ref\": \"F000\",\n      \"scope_refs\": [],\n      \"kind\": \"requirement\",\n      \"meaning\": \"If an employer does not maintain an accurate record of hours worked by an employee—including employees exempt from the Fair Labor Standards Act's (FLSA) requirement that hours worked be recorded (such as bona fide executive, administrative, and professional employees defined in 29 CFR part 541)—the employer bears the burden of showing that the employee has not worked the requisite hours.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"quote_ref\": \"F000\",\n      \"scope_refs\": [],\n      \"kind\": \"requirement\",\n      \"meaning\": \"Regardless of whether an employer maintains accurate records of hours worked, an employer must be able to clearly demonstrate that full-time teachers (as defined in § 825.102) of an elementary or secondary school system, institution of higher education, or other educational establishment or institution (who often work outside the classroom or at home) did not work 1,250 hours during the preceding 12 months in order to claim that the teachers are not eligible for FMLA leave (stated as an example).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"quote_ref\": \"F000\",\n      \"scope_refs\": [],\n      \"kind\": \"background\",\n      \"meaning\": \"Provides a cross-reference directing readers to § 825.801(d) for special rules applicable to airline flight crew employees, conveying no substantive requirement or limitation on its own.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
